      "id": 1,
      "text": "Founded in 1889, Melville earned the nickname Atchafalaya River Catfish Capital of Louisiana.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melville%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Historically, the town made its fortune in river commerce and later became a railroad crossing point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cajuntravel.com/destinations/melville/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Melville sits on flat land surrounded by a ring levee protecting it from flooding by the Atchafalaya River and West Atchafalaya Floodway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melville%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the early 1900s, Melville operated several fish docks and ice houses, shipping 50 barrels of fish daily.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cajuntravel.com/destinations/melville/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Melville prides itself on family-oriented community values, with small-town charm and friendly people.",
